ui: add light theme with OSC 11 auto-detection and a /theme picker

Light and dark palettes now share ANSI base-16 accents so indicators
follow whatever palette the terminal carries; the rest of the palette
pins explicit 256-index tones per-polarity. Auto (default) probes the
terminal background via OSC 11 and falls back to dark when there is no
reply. [ui] theme = ... persists in config; /theme switches for the
rest of the session only and re-runs the probe when Auto is picked.
Switching themes clears the frozen-render cache so previously styled
turns repaint under the new palette.

INPUT chip renders quietly (muted-on-panel) rather than as an accent
background; the muted mid-gray clashes with fg under either theme
polarity and only worked pre-light-theme by accident of which tones
were paired.